# ── seller.gopasal.com (seller console) ───────────────────────────────────────
# Copy to `.env.local`. Everything here is NEXT_PUBLIC_*, i.e. it ships to the
# browser: put only publishable values in this file. Secrets belong in
# apps/api/.env.

# The GoPasal API's origin — no path, no trailing slash. The console appends
# /api/v1 itself, so a future API version is a code change, not a config change.
#
# Unlike the customer site, this console has no sample-data mode: sign-in,
# sessions and the shop application are all real API calls. With this unset every
# screen says the console is not connected instead of showing invented data.
NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL=http://localhost:4000

# There is deliberately no NEXT_PUBLIC_SELLER_URL here. One was listed, described
# as "used for canonical links", and nothing read it: the console's canonical
# origin is pinned in `app/layout.tsx` as `metadataBase`. Setting the variable
# changed nothing, which is the worst kind of configuration — it looks answered.
# Moving that origin is a one-line code change in that file.

# Extra hosts `next/image` may fetch product photos from, comma-separated
# (`cdn.gopasal.com` or `https://bucket.s3.ap-south-1.amazonaws.com`). Needed only
# when the API's storage provider is `s3`, or when STORAGE_LOCAL_PUBLIC_BASE_URL
# points somewhere other than the API origin — in that case `publicUrl` returns a
# host this console cannot infer. NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL's host is always allowed, so
# leave this unset in local development.
#
# Anything not listed here is refused by the image optimiser rather than proxied.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_IMAGE_HOSTS=
